<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Multi-channel grouping</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Random grouping</h3>

<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2511.23142v1/images/multi-channel-sampling.png" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/199;" width="476" height="199" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A1.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Random subset of 4 channels with pivot Cz on the 10-20 System. On the left, the induced probability distribution from pivot Cz. On the right, the sampled channels.. <em id="A1.F4.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Adapted from</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. Public domain.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We outline here the <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">random groups</em> sampling procedure employed during fine-tuning. For a given EEG recording, we start with all EEG channels <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>, each with a 3D scalp location
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{c}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{c}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> on the unit sphere (<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}_{c}\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}_{c}\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>). We keep a pool
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> of channels not yet assigned, and build groups <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1},G_{2},\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1},G_{2},\dots</annotation></semantics></math> until
<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is empty.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1) Pick a group size (1–5).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each group, draw <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mathrm{Exp}(\lambda=3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mathrm{Exp}(\lambda=3)</annotation></semantics></math>, round up, and clip to the range <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,5]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;=\;\min\{5,\,\max\{1,\,\lceil X\rceil\}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>5</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;=\;\min\{5,\,\max\{1,\,\lceil X\rceil\}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, make sure we don’t ask for more channels than remain: <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leftarrow\min\{s,\;|\mathcal{R}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leftarrow\min\{s,\;|\mathcal{R}|\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(If you want larger or smaller typical groups, scale <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> before rounding.)</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Manual grouping</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We outline here the <em id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">manual groups</em> crafted for the multi-channel EEG reconstruction for the epilepsy and anomaly detection tasks.</p>
