<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A1.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Manual channel groups for the TUAB (Abnormal EEG) task.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2) Choose a pivot.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pick one pivot channel <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly at random from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and put it in the group (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\leftarrow\{p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\leftarrow\{p\}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">3) Fill the rest by proximity.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each candidate <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{R}\setminus G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{R}\setminus G</annotation></semantics></math>, compute its distance to the pivot
(using chord distance on the unit sphere, which has the property of being monotonic with the geodesic angle):</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(p,c)\;=\;\|\mathbf{x}_{p}-\mathbf{x}_{c}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(p,c)\;=\;\|\mathbf{x}_{p}-\mathbf{x}_{c}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Turn distances into sampling weights so nearer channels are more likely:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{c}=\exp\!\left(-\frac{d(p,c)}{\tau}\right),\qquad\pi(c\mid p)=\frac{w_{c}}{\sum_{c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}\setminus G}w_{c^{\prime}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{c}=\exp\!\left(-\frac{d(p,c)}{\tau}\right),\qquad\pi(c\mid p)=\frac{w_{c}}{\sum_{c^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}\setminus G}w_{c^{\prime}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Sample <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s-1</annotation></semantics></math> distinct neighbors without replacement from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\setminus G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\setminus G</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\mid p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\mid p)</annotation></semantics></math>,
add them to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, remove <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and repeat. We set the temperature <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>DAC-DC Reconstructions</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we give example reconstructions of 5 neighboring channels with DAC-MC.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2511.23142v1/5channel.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/129;" width="471" height="129" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example reconstruction with fine-tuned codec with multi-channels.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
</div>
